From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:57:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: apple,dcp: name the display pipe's PMC
 interface

A DCP that powers its display domains down while the display is off
clears its pipe's PMC interface enables first and restores them after
powering the domains up. Add apple,pmc-interface, a phandle to the pipe's
apple,consumer-switched PMC interface node.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit e3c8b69fabbf9bb6a4769e274963cd90120513be)
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
index 66e341e7e9..75d7f31cb5 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
@@ -243,6 +243,14 @@ properties:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
     description: Height in pixels reserved for the display notch.
 
+  apple,pmc-interface:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      The PMC interface enables of this coprocessor's display pipe, an
+      apple,consumer-switched interface node. The coprocessor clears them
+      before it powers its display domains down while the display is off,
+      and restores them after it powers them up again.
+
   apple,pmp-report:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
     description:
